 "news": {
  "date": "2026-09-07",
  "asof": "2026-09-08 09:15 UTC",
  "headline": "No session, and crude broke out anyway \u2014 the transmission this brief called broken is back",
  "standfirst": "Monday was Labor Day and US markets did not open, so every price in the pack is Friday 4 September's carried forward and there is no tape to read. What moved was the thing the tape cannot show: Brent reached about $97 and WTI $92.27 on Monday, both six-week highs, with an average of roughly ten ships a day crossing the Strait of Hormuz (Al Jazeera) \u2014 Phoenix's own WTI still reads 91.48 because that is Friday's close. Crude feeds CPI, CPI is the gate holding this regime, and it prints on Friday. In the book, nothing changed: heat is still 3.16R against a 3.0R cap and flagged over cap, and Apple reports tomorrow with no stop on the position.",
  "themes": [],
  "ondeck": "Apple's product event is tomorrow, Wednesday 9 September; August CPI lands Friday 11 September at 08:30 ET and is the regime's tightest gate; the FOMC meets 15\u201316 September; triple witching is 18 September.",
  "note": null
 },
